            <ArticleTitle>Thoracoscopic biopsy of a pathological vertebral body.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>726-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>When computed tomography (CT) guided biopsy of a pathological vertebral body fails, the accepted alternative has been open thoracotomy and biopsy. The authors wish to report the use of a thoracoscopic approach to biopsy of a pathological thoracic vertebra in a child, after an unsuccessful attempt at CT guided percutaneous biopsy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
